      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "After a season that ended with the Leafs sitting 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, the team is now aggressively reshaping its roster for a Cup push. <strong>GM John Chayka confirmed a busy Canada Day, adding seven new players including Sergei Bobrovsky and Nick Paul, while trading Dennis Hildeby to Tampa Bay.</strong> The front office is clearly embracing a \"star-hunt\" philosophy, a move that has drawn praise for its bold IQ and immediate impact. Newcomer Gavin McKenna, the draft's first overall pick, is already making waves with his first ice session in Toronto, signaling a new era of youthful energy. The cap space is being deployed with precision, and the roster is being built to compete, not just participate. <strong>What to watch next is how quickly Bobrovsky and the new additions integrate before training camp opens, as that will define the Leafs' ceiling for 2026-27.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 3, 2026"
      },
