        "body": "Toronto Blue Jays aren't playing sloppy baseball; they're finally showing contender grit after a mixed bag of results. The most telling moment came when rookie Sean Keys launched his first Major League home run, sparking a <strong>9-3 victory over the Mets on Canada Day</strong> that ended a two-game slump. Now sitting 41-46 and third in the AL East, the Jays are 11.5 games behind but riding a W1 streak, proving they can punch back when needed. Keys stepping in as DH on short notice and delivering a show-for-Canada performance signals a young core ready to surge. With Dylan Cease on the mound next, the team faces a critical test against Seattle. <strong>The Jays must capitalize on Saturday's 10:10 PM ET game at the Mariners to keep their playoff hunt alive and close the gap on the division leaders.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 3, 2026"
