        "body": "The Toronto Raptors aren't just reshaping their roster; they're reigniting a legacy with Kawhi Leonard back in the fold and Kyle Lowry's emotional retirement as a one-day signing. <strong>Kawhi Leonard's return to Toronto for Brandon Ingram, Gradey Dick, two first-round picks, a swap, and second-rounders</strong> transforms a 46-36 team into a genuine Eastern Conference contender overnight. This isn't nostalgia - it's strategy. The front office, armed with cap flexibility and two-way spots, now eyes adding depth to complement Leonard and Scottie Barnes, while Kyle Anderson's one-year, $3.9 million veteran minimum deal (counting as $2.4 million for cap) fills a critical rotation void. The season's end, finalized in third place in the Atlantic, was merely the pause before the sprint. <strong>What to watch: Can the Raptors secure a third star to pair with Kawhi and Barnes before camp opens, and will Lowry's retirement spark a cultural reset that pushes them past the Celtics?</strong>",
